+# `CHOL` answered 13457-7, calculated LDL. The key posts 178 rows, and LDL,
+# HDL, total cholesterol and their ratio tie on commonness, so the first row
+# won. A slip's CHOL column is total cholesterol, like TC above; `总胆固醇
+# (CHOL)` was refused as two analytes. The trailing-token guard then stops
+# cutting `LDL-CHOL` to `LDL`, its halves now differing, so hyphenated
+# spellings get rows. A spaced row would also catch `CHOL/HDL`, a ratio.
+CHOL	Cholesterol
+LDL-CHOL	LDL-C
+HDL-CHOL	HDL-C
+CHOL-LDL	LDL-C
